# Generated scan artifacts inside fixtures (review/report/baseline JSON produced by
# running the gate against a fixture — these embed local paths and scan evidence and
# must never be committed). The top-level .mcp/* rules above are anchored to the repo
# root, so fixture copies need their own patterns.
fixtures/**/.mcp/baselines/
fixtures/**/.mcp/reviews/
fixtures/**/.mcp/reports/

# Internal-only documents — engineering/advisory notes and pitch material that must
# stay local and never reach the public GitHub repo or the npm package. The public
# docs (README.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, docs/WIKI.md) are intentionally NOT listed.
docs/SECURITY_GAP_ANALYSIS.md
docs/UPGRADE_BUILD_INSTRUCTIONS.md
security-mcp-deck-prompt.md

# Keep the intentional malicious-agent test fixtures (consumed by src/tests/run.ts).
# These live under .claude/ but must be tracked so CI's npm test can detect them.
!fixtures/agentic-malicious/.claude/
!fixtures/agentic-malicious/.claude/**

# Generated executive deck (binary, regenerated from security-mcp-deck-prompt.md)
